  "content": {
    "title": "TGL Finals results: LA takes first game vs. Tiger Woods' Jupiter Links",
    "text": "Updated March 23, 2026, 11:21 p.m. ETSoon the final hammer will be thrown and a new winner will be crowned as the second TGL season comes to a close. A two-day finals finds Jupiter Links GC, led by Tiger Woods, taking on the Los Angeles Golf Club.Taking the first win of the best-of-three series was Los Angeles, who survived a neck-to-neck, back-and-forth battle against Jupiter, 6-5.It was ultimately decided in the final hole during a singles match of Kevin Kisner versus Sahith Theegala. Kisner barely missed a 21-foot putt from the green after Los Angeles initiated a hammer throw to make the final hole worth two points.Jupiter Links led 5-4 going into Hole 19.Jupiter found its way to the finals after besting Rory McIlroy's Boston Commons last week, 9-5, taking down the No. 1 team on the season. LA's contingent of Tommy Fleetwood, Sahith Theegala and Justin Rose got the better of Atlanta Drive in the semifinals and is just two wins from glory.The star of the show remains Woods, who is still sidelined after back surgery in October. However, he is expected to be a vocal supporter from the sidelines.The playoff bracket concludes with a two-day, best-of-three format. Monday tees off the action with a one-match event, followed by a possible two-match extravaganza on Tuesday.USA TODAY Sports has you covered on updates and results, here's how the action went on Monday: Things get interesting down the stretchIt was an amazing showcase as each golfer went putt for putt, tee for tee, birdie for birdie. Jupiter even tried to throw a hammer, but LA accepted it. It came down to a six-foot putt for Jupiter and a four-foot putt for LA. Kim and Fleetwood put on a masterclass. Kim made his putt and screamed \"this is my house\" to the attendees. Fleetwood came over calm, cool and collected hit his putt to tie Hole 14. Jupiter maintained its 5-4 lead.Going into Hole 15, LA opened with a hammer throw. Jupiter Link accepted, so the hole is worth two points. It was Kisner versus Theegala. And it was close, but in the end Kisner barely missed a 21-foot putt from the green. LA took the 6-5 win. LAGC leads the best-of-three series 1-0. Max Homa takes over Hole 13Homa gave Jupiter the 5-4 lead with a takeover of the 13th hole. Homa drove the green on TGL's Cut The Sails course, he went for 336 yards to 40-feet. It is the first time anyone has driven the green on Cut The Sails.He then redeemed his Hole 10 blunder with the same three-foot birdie, except he sank it in Hole 13. LA took a short lead in Hole 11, tied in 12thLA Golf Club took a 4-3 after throwing a hammer that Jupiter denied, forfeiting a point. In the following hole, Kisner got a good initial virtual tee off for Jupiter Links. He then proceeded to show off his dance moves. Ultimately, LA would concede the entire hole allowing Jupiter to knot it up, 4-4, after Hole 12. Rose defeats King of singles match in Hole 10Homa has won six consecutive singles matches in 2026, the most in TGL history. He went against Justin Rose in Hole 10, the first hole of singles, and his streak was snapped seven. Rose connected on a birdie to win the hole and it was left to Homa to try and tie. He just missed a three-foot birdie, which ringed out.LAGC tied the match at three, apiece. Jupiter throws hammer, snatches lead into singlesJupiter Links lead Tiger Woods made an executive decision to throw the hammer and put pressure on Los Angeles. LA declined the hammer, conceding points and the hole. Jupiter Links would go ahead, 3-2, after Hole 9 as the teams head into singles. Justin Rose ties it with skillful birdieJustin Rose showed why he's one of the top 10 golfers in the world. Rose tied the game in Hole 8 with one of the more skilled shots of the evening, a birdie from off of the edge of the grass. Sinker.Rose in celebration, slapped fives with his team and blew a kiss and pointed to his wife in attendance. Kim big birdie from eight feet takes advantageTom Kim hit a huge birdie from about eight feel to give Jupiter Links a, 2-1, lead after Hole 7. LAGC missed three consecutive short range pars from about eight-feet out, each. Afterwards, Kim looked at his opponents and shrugged as if to say, \"what?\". Kisner can't tie the game in Hole 5, catches break in Hole 6Kevin Kisner had a chance to tie the match with a 15-foot par shot. It veered slightly off. The shot would have won the hole for Jupiter Links. They remained down 1-0 through Hole 5.On to Hole 6.Tom Kim missed par for Jupiter. Fleetwood wasn't able to connect on a birdie. Kisner had a chance to win the hole with a six-foot birdie, but he limped it.However, Kisner and Jupiter caught a break when Theegala missed on his chance to win the hold. The score was tied going into Hole 7. Theegala comes up short, Homa keeps Jupiter closeSahith Theegala had a chance to extend the LAGC lead but came up just centimeters short on an eagle shot. It set up an opportunity for Jupiter Links' Max Homa to make an eight-foot shot and keep the score at 1-0 through Hole 4. LA takes first lead against Jupiter LinksThe TGL Finals between LA Golf Club and Jupiter Links was even through the first hole, but it was LA who opened the match with the first points. Tom Kim missed a 19-foot birdie that would have given Jupiter a lead.Instead, Tommy Fleetwood led with a deep shot through the caverns and set up good positioning for the next shot. He capped his turn with chip shot that gave LAGC a 1-0 lead after Hole 2.LA's 1-0 lead remained in tact after Hole 3.TGL playoff finals: TV, time and how to watch MondayMatch 1: Jupiter Links GC vs. Los Angeles Golf ClubDate: Monday, March 23Time: 9 p.m. ETTV: ESPN2Stream: Fubo, ESPN+Watch the TGL Finals on FuboMatch 2: Los Angeles Golf Club vs. Jupiter Links GCDate: Tuesday, March 24Time: 7 p.m. ETTV: ESPNStream: Fubo, ESPN+Match 3: Los Angeles Golf Club vs. Jupiter Links GC (if necessary)Date: Tuesday, March 24Time: 9 p.m. ETTV: ESPNStream: Fubo, ESPN+",
